  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: netty-codec-http2 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released io.netty:netty-codec-http2 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001 with backported fixes for CVE-2025-55163, CVE-2026-33871, CVE-2026-42587, CVE-2026-47244, CVE-2026-48043, CVE-2026-50560, CVE-2026-56819, and CVE-2026-59900.\n\nCVE-2025-55163: Netty MadeYouReset HTTP/2 DDoS Vulnerability\n\nCVE-2026-33871: Netty HTTP/2 CONTINUATION Frame Flood DoS via Zero-Byte Frame Bypass\n\nCVE-2026-42587: Netty: HttpContentDecompressor maxAllocation bypass via Content-Encoding: br/zstd/snappy enables decompression bomb DoS\n\nCVE-2026-47244: Netty HTTP/2: Advertised MAX_CONCURRENT_STREAMS are not enforced\n\nCVE-2026-48043: netty-codec-http2: ByteBuf Reference-Count Leak in DelegatingDecompressorFrameListener Leads to Memory Exhaustion\n\nCVE-2026-50560: Netty susceptible to HTTP/2 Reset Attack with different on-the-wire signature\n\nCVE-2026-56819: Netty: HTTP/2 decompression leaks ByteBuf reference count when the decompressor channel is already closed (Direct memory leak / OOM DoS)\n\nCVE-2026-59900: Netty codec-http2: Lack of Host Header Deduplication in HTTP/2\u2192HTTP/1.x Translation Leads to Request Routing Bypass\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for io.netty:netty-codec-http2 4.1.100.Final from Maven Central.",
